It began as a re-architecture of go-jupyter by the Gene Ontology Consortium:

    https://github.com/geneontology/go-jupyter

Most of the Claude Code first-run state seeding in student-image/seed-home.sh
came from that project — the settings that suppress first-run prompts, and the
technique of pre-approving an injected API key by its last 20 characters. Their
published workshop write-up also supplied findings this project acts on: per-user
tool caches driving disk requirements, context carried between exercises
triggering compaction, and model API spend dwarfing infrastructure cost.

